<title>PORTUGAL: J. Martins share trade suspension lifted.</title>
<headline>J. Martins share trade suspension lifted.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lisbon bourse has lifted a suspension imposed on Thursday on the trade of shares in retailer Jeronimo Martins, a bourse spokesman said on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are lifting the suspension...because investors now have sufficient information about the negotiations with Vidago,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Jeronimo Martins &amp; Filho-SGPS issued a statement on Thursday saying that it was studying the possibility of launching a public offer to buy the mineral water group.</p>
<p>Trade in its shares had been halted after press reports that it was preparing a bid.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
